The date reports merged into #4471 do not describe one bug. Tenant locale, booking-form
version, and channel separate them into two causes. The table below deduplicates overlapping
export rows by report ID, then classifies each report from its tenant and submission path.

## Cause breakdown

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The shared parser reads month first, but day-first tenants expect day first. A separate form
problem affects day-first tenants using booking-v3: its `MM/DD/YYYY` hint conflicts with their
day-first date handling. Intake tags describe the initial guess, not the cause, so they are
shown for comparison rather than used to group reports.

The desk's one-day-move notes (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, and R-41620) are evidence
within the parser group, not a third cause.

## How the desk should use this split

The [subject-only merge rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) is not reliable for these reports.
The existing classifier and triage explorer compare causes instead: the same subject can
describe different problems, and different subjects can describe the same problem.

- A booking-v3 form report from alder.physio and an app report from the same tenant belong
  to different causes, even when both say "Booking on the wrong date".
- Booking-v3 form reports from pale.harbour and alder.physio share the hint cause, even
  when their subjects differ.
- Without tenant metadata, the cause is unknown. Do not merge on a matching subject alone;
  first establish the tenant, locale, form version, and channel.

The accepted historical [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is preserved
as evidence of the old rule. This page documents the contrary evidence for #4471; it does
not claim that the desk has accepted a replacement policy.

## Resolution record

This page completes the analysis of the exported reports, not a product-code fix.
The linked issues track the parser and hint findings separately. Their resolution should
link to this signed page and its rendered snapshot so that the desk can check the evidence.

The export is a snapshot dated 2026-10-04. Before treating either product problem as fixed,
the desk must check its current reports and fix status. A closed analysis issue is not
evidence that the parser or booking form has been repaired.

